# Styleguide Review Cadence

When working on a project, periodically compare implementation choices against
the local styleguide before finalizing meaningful changes.

Especially after a commit, before a push, or when resuming work after a few
hours:

- Re-read or recall the relevant styleguide rules.
- Check whether changed files still communicate the intended project style.
- Treat the styleguide as guidance, not a rigid formatter.
- Preserve user-introduced naturalness when it improves readability.
- Call out style drift only when it harms clarity, consistency, or intent.

For this project, prefer light horizontal density, vertical step-by-step code,
clear contracts, and readable OOP over production-style cleverness.
